From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pletch <17855860+pletch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:48:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dummynet_st: release packets between ticks

The second of the sub-tick release series (opnsense-cake SUBTICK.md). A
pipe's times go from ticks to microseconds of uptime: the scheduler
instances' credit (now bits * DN_CREDIT_HZ, 10^6), sched_time and
idle_time, the packets' output times, the event heap's keys and the
link's delay. curr_time stays in ticks for the AQMs and RED.

With net.inet.ip.dummynet.release_us below the tick, the heap's keys are
rounded up to a grid of release_us, and a callout at the first key,
armed whenever it moves earlier, queues dummynet_fine_task, which serves
the heap and arms it again; the tick task carries on as before and
serves the heap too, so a missed wakeup waits a tick at most. At the
tick (the default) no callout is armed and releases go by the tick.

The packet that takes a pipe's credit below zero now leaves at once, as
from sch_cake's shaper, rather than when it is paid for, and an idle
pipe starts at no credit rather than io_fast's tick: with credit in us,
holding the packet would delay every packet of a sparse flow by its own
time and the grid. release_catchup_us caps the credit a pipe gains in
one release (0, the default: all it is owed). release_wakeups,
release_pkts, release_late_us, release_late_max and release_catchups
count the releases between ticks. net.inet.ip.dummynet.subtick is 2.
